<title>BELGIUM: Belgian industrial production index rises in Feb.</title>
<headline>Belgian industrial production index rises in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Statistics Office released the following indices for production in industry excluding the construction sector -</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	    Feb 97     Jan 97	  Feb 96</p>
<p> work day index (1990=100) (*)   104.5	92.7	    100.9</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) index per working day, adjusted for length and composition of the months  </p>
<p> SEASONALLY ADJUSTED INDICES(*) Feb 97     Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> industry as a whole		 95.1	 94.5	  93.6</p>
<p> construction industry	     77.7	 76.1	  76.9</p>
<p> investment goods		   100.5	 99.8	  99.1</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) seasonally adjusted based on averages of the last 12 months.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
